<section class="content-ui-section" style="padding: 55px 0; background: #0b132b; color: #cbd5e1; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07);">
  <div class="container" style="max-width: 1060px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 15px;">
    <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.65); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 16px; padding: 36px 32px; box-shadow: 0 12px 30px rgba(0,0,0,0.35);">
      <span style="background: rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.12); color: #f59e0b; border: 1px solid rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.35); padding: 4px 14px; border-radius: 20px; font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px; display: inline-block; margin-bottom: 14px;">HANDOVER INSPECTION</span>
      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Destination Handover, Odometer Sign-Off &amp; Joint Condition Inspection for Car Transport From Bhubaneswar To Hyderabad</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">The destination delivery handover for an automobile or car is a critical checkpoint that confirms the vehicle’s condition, mileage, and paperwork match the expectations set at pickup.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>Conducting a thorough daylight re‑inspection, verifying the odometer against the LR (Logistics Receipt) bilty, and obtaining a signed condition sign‑off ensures transparency for both the carrier and the receiver.</span></li></ul>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Daylight Condition Re‑inspection</strong>
    <ul>
      <li>Schedule the inspection in natural daylight to reveal any surface damage, dents, scratches, or interior wear that artificial lighting might obscure.</li>
      <li>Bring the original pickup photographs and compare each angle (front, rear, sides, roof, interior) with the vehicle’s current state.</li>
      <li>Use a standardized checklist to note discrepancies, such as new dents, broken glass, or interior stains, and photograph any new issues for the record.</li>
      <li>Confirm that all accessories (spare tire, jack, owner’s manual) are present and undamaged.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>

  <li><strong>Odometer Verification Against LR Bilty</strong>
    <ul>
      <li>Locate the odometer reading on the vehicle and record it to the nearest whole mile/kilometer.</li>
      <li>Cross‑reference this reading with the mileage listed on the LR bilty (the logistics receipt completed at pickup).</li>
      <li>If the reading exceeds the bilty mileage, calculate the variance and document the cause (e.g., test drive, routing detour).</li>
      <li>Note any tampering signs, such as mismatched digits or abnormal wear on the odometer glass.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>

  <li><strong>Signed Condition Sign‑off</strong>
    <ul>
      <li>Present the inspection checklist, comparison photos, and odometer verification to the receiver.</li>
      <li>Both parties review each item, discuss any discrepancies, and agree on the vehicle’s final condition.</li>
      <li>The receiver signs the checklist, confirming acceptance of the vehicle as inspected; the carrier signs to acknowledge the handover.</li>
      <li>Provide a copy of the signed document, photos, and the LR bilty to the receiver for their records.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
</ul>

<p>By following these steps—daylight re‑inspection, precise odometer verification, and a documented signed sign‑off—both parties protect themselves from disputes, ensure accurate mileage reporting, and maintain a clear audit trail for the automobile’s journey from pickup to final delivery.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>



